        "title": "Crop Systems - Monoculture, Rotation, Cover Crops, Agroforestry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "How crops are arranged in space and time determines pest pressure, nutrient cycling, water use, soil health, and resilience. Industrial agriculture converged on monoculture because it maximizes mechanization efficiency. The cost: ecosystem services lost, external inputs required, vulnerability to pests and climate. The trend is toward diversified systems that recover those services without sacrificing productivity."
    },
