        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Crop Systems - Monoculture, Rotation, Cover Crops, Agroforestry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCROP SYSTEM                   DISTRIBUTED SYSTEMS EQUIVALENT\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nMONOCULTURE                   Single point of failure (SPOF) architecture\n  One species over large area  → Single service with no redundancy\n  Uniform genetic base         → Identical replicas: same vulnerability in all\n  One pest adaptation kills all→ Exploit that works on one instance works on all\n  Irish Potato Famine 1845:   → Production outage: all replicas fail simultaneously\n    one pathogen (Phytophthora)\n    → nation-wide crop failure\n  Advantage: mechanization    → Operational simplicity; single deployment target\n    efficiency, low overhead    horizontal scaling is trivial if nothing goes wrong"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-CROP-SYSTEMS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "02-CROP-SYSTEMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:agriculture:02-crop-systems, git-history:agriculture:02-crop-systems]",
