        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Crop Systems - Monoculture, Rotation, Cover Crops, Agroforestry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "POLYCULTURE / ROTATION         Fault-tolerant distributed architecture\n  Multiple species / timing    → Service redundancy + diverse failure modes\n  Pest can't adapt to all      → No single vulnerability cascades to total failure\n  N-fixing legumes in rotation → Shared infrastructure (legume = free N source)\n    reduce external input need   for subsequent crop, like shared caching layer\n  \"Portfolio diversification\"  → Multiple uncorrelated risk streams; variance ↓\n  Cost: complexity             → Higher operational overhead; scheduling complexity"
    },
